<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>eu.nosini.Pulsemeeter</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>
  <name>Pulsemeeter</name>
  <summary>Route audio between virtual and hardware devices</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.therealcarneiro">
    <name>Gabriel Carneiro</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Pulsemeeter is a mixer for PipeWire with a workflow similar to
      Voicemeeter. It creates virtual inputs and outputs and lets you route
      any input to any output, whether the device is hardware or virtual.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Create virtual inputs and outputs</li>
      <li>Route audio from input devices to output devices</li>
      <li>Volume and mute control, with optional per-route volume</li>
      <li>Channel layouts for virtual devices (mono, stereo and more)</li>
      <li>Port selection for hardware devices</li>
      <li>Custom port-to-port connection mapping</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Pulsemeeter requires PipeWire with pipewire-pulse. This is an
      unofficial Flatpak build of the upstream project.
    </p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">eu.nosini.Pulsemeeter.desktop</launchable>
